{
  "info": {
    "name": "Application Health",
    "description": "Comprehensive health monitoring for all Spring AI Course modules\n\n## Learning Objectives\n- Understand health check patterns in microservices and modular applications\n- Learn Spring Boot Actuator integration for monitoring\n- Explore module-specific health indicators\n- Practice production monitoring and alerting patterns\n\n## Why Health Checks Are Critical\nHealth checks are essential for production applications, enabling:\n- **Load balancer integration**: Remove unhealthy instances from traffic\n- **Container orchestration**: Kubernetes liveness and readiness probes\n- **Monitoring and alerting**: Automated detection of service issues\n- **Debugging and troubleshooting**: Quick status overview across modules\n\n## Health Check Architecture\n- **Application-level**: Overall application health and configuration\n- **Module-level**: Individual feature health and dependencies\n- **Component-level**: Database, AI service, and external dependency health\n- **Custom indicators**: Business-specific health metrics\n\n## Production Monitoring Patterns\n- Centralized health dashboard\n- Automated alerting on health failures\n- Health check aggregation and correlation\n- Performance impact monitoring\n\n## Testing Prerequisites\n- Application running: `./mvnw spring-boot:run`\n- All modules properly configured\n- OpenAI API key available (for AI-dependent health checks)",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_postman_id": "application-health",
    "version": {
      "major": 1,
      "minor": 0,
      "patch": 0
    }
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Application Level Health",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Main Application Health",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/health",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "health"]
            },
            "description": "Main application health endpoint providing overview of all modules.\n\n**Why application-level health is important:**\n- **Single entry point**: Quick overall status check\n- **Module aggregation**: Summary of all module health states\n- **Load balancer integration**: Simple UP/DOWN status for traffic routing\n- **Operational overview**: High-level view for operations teams\n\n**Health check implementation patterns:**\n- **Composite health indicator**: Aggregates multiple module health checks\n- **Fast response**: Should respond quickly even under load\n- **Dependency awareness**: Reflects critical dependency status\n- **Graceful degradation**: Partial functionality vs complete failure\n\n**Production considerations:**\n- Configure appropriate timeouts for health checks\n- Include version information for deployment tracking\n- Monitor health check response times\n- Set up alerting for health check failures\n\n**Integration with infrastructure:**\n- **Kubernetes**: Use for liveness and readiness probes\n- **Load balancers**: Configure health check paths\n- **Monitoring tools**: Prometheus, Grafana, etc.\n- **Service mesh**: Istio, Linkerd health integration"
          },
          "response": [
            {
              "name": "Healthy Response",
              "originalRequest": {
                "method": "GET",
                "header": [],
                "url": {
                  "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/health",
                  "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
                  "path": ["api", "health"]
                }
              },
              "status": "OK",
              "code": 200,
              "_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
              "header": [
                {
                  "key": "Content-Type",
                  "value": "application/json"
                }
              ],
              "cookie": [],
              "body": "{\n  \"status\": \"UP\",\n  \"application\": \"Spring AI Course - L4AiChat\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n  \"modules\": {\n    \"s1-multiturn\": \"UP\",\n    \"s2-components\": \"UP\",\n    \"s3-context\": \"UP\",\n    \"s4-statemanagement\": \"UP\",\n    \"s5-chatbot\": \"UP\",\n    \"s6-advanced\": \"UP\",\n    \"s7-advisors\": \"UP\",\n    \"s8-multimodel\": \"UP\",\n    \"s9-templates\": \"UP\"\n  },\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"openai-api\": \"CONNECTED\",\n    \"database\": \"UP\",\n    \"memory\": \"HEALTHY\"\n  },\n  \"timestamp\": \"2024-01-01T10:00:00Z\"\n}"
            }
          ],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Application health status is UP\", function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.status).to.eql(\"UP\");",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test(\"All modules are healthy\", function () {",
                  "    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('modules');",
                  "    ",
                  "    // Check that all modules are UP",
                  "    Object.keys(jsonData.modules).forEach(function(module) {",
                  "        pm.expect(jsonData.modules[module]).to.eql('UP');",
                  "    });",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test(\"Dependencies are healthy\", function () {",
                  "    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('dependencies');",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.dependencies).to.have.property('database');",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.dependencies).to.have.property('memory');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test(\"Response time is acceptable for health check\", function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.responseTime).to.be.below(5000);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test(\"Application version is provided\", function () {",
                  "    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('version');",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.version).to.be.a('string');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "description": "Application-level health checks for overall system status"
    },
