    {
      "name": "Health Check Workflows",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Complete Health Check Suite",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/health",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "health"]
            },
            "description": "Run complete health check workflow to verify all systems."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "// Initialize health check workflow",
                  "console.log('Starting complete health check suite...');",
                  "pm.environment.set('healthCheckStartTime', new Date().toISOString());"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "// Main application health validation",
                  "pm.test(\"Main application health check passed\", function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.status).to.eql(\"UP\");",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "// Chain to module health checks",
                  "pm.test(\"Prepare for module health checks\", function () {",
                  "    var modules = pm.response.json().modules;",
                  "    var moduleList = Object.keys(modules);",
                  "    pm.environment.set('modulesToCheck', JSON.stringify(moduleList));",
                  "    pm.environment.set('currentModuleIndex', '0');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "// Set up next request in workflow",
                  "var modules = JSON.parse(pm.environment.get('modulesToCheck') || '[]');",
                  "if (modules.length > 0) {",
                  "    var firstModule = modules[0].replace('-', '').replace('multiturn', '').replace('components', '').replace('context', '').replace('statemanagement', '').replace('chatbot', '').replace('advanced', '').replace('advisors', '').replace('multimodel', '').replace('templates', '');",
                  "    console.log('Next: Check module health endpoints');",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Health Monitoring Dashboard Data",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/health",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "health"]
            },
            "description": "Simulates health monitoring dashboard data collection.\n\n**Dashboard monitoring patterns:**\n- **Real-time status**: Current health state of all modules\n- **Historical data**: Health trends over time\n- **Alert integration**: Trigger notifications on health changes\n- **Dependency mapping**: Visualize service dependencies\n\n**Key metrics to track:**\n- Module availability percentage\n- Response time trends\n- Error rates and patterns\n- Resource utilization correlation\n\n**Production dashboard features:**\n- Color-coded health status visualization\n- Drill-down capability to module details\n- Historical health trend charts\n- Alert acknowledgment and escalation\n\n**Integration with monitoring tools:**\n- Prometheus metrics export\n- Grafana dashboard integration\n- PagerDuty/OpsGenie alerting\n- Slack/Teams notifications"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Dashboard data collection successful\", function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "    ",
                  "    // Simulate dashboard data processing",
                  "    var dashboardData = {",
                  "        timestamp: jsonData.timestamp,",
                  "        overallStatus: jsonData.status,",
                  "        moduleCount: Object.keys(jsonData.modules).length,",
                  "        healthyModules: Object.values(jsonData.modules).filter(status => status === 'UP').length,",
                  "        responseTime: pm.response.responseTime",
                  "    };",
                  "    ",
                  "    pm.environment.set('dashboardData', JSON.stringify(dashboardData));",
                  "    ",
                  "    // Validate dashboard data",
                  "    pm.expect(dashboardData.overallStatus).to.eql('UP');",
                  "    pm.expect(dashboardData.healthyModules).to.eql(dashboardData.moduleCount);",
                  "    pm.expect(dashboardData.responseTime).to.be.below(5000);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test(\"All modules available for dashboard\", function () {",
                  "    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "    var moduleCount = Object.keys(jsonData.modules).length;",
                  "    pm.expect(moduleCount).to.be.greaterThan(5); // Expecting at least 6 modules",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "description": "Health check workflows and monitoring patterns"
    },
    {
      "name": "Error Scenarios",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Simulated Unhealthy Module",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/nonexistent/health",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "nonexistent", "health"]
            },
            "description": "Tests error handling for non-existent module health checks.\n\n**Why error scenario testing is important:**\n- **Graceful degradation**: System continues operating with partial functionality\n- **Alert validation**: Ensure monitoring systems detect failures correctly\n- **Recovery procedures**: Test restoration workflows\n- **Client resilience**: Validate client handling of health check failures\n\n**Common health check failure scenarios:**\n- Module temporarily unavailable\n- Database connectivity issues\n- External service dependencies down\n- Resource exhaustion (memory, CPU)\n- Configuration errors\n\n**Error response patterns:**\n- Appropriate HTTP status codes (503 Service Unavailable)\n- Detailed error information for debugging\n- Partial health information when possible\n- Clear indication of affected functionality\n\n**Production error handling:**\n- Circuit breaker patterns for failing dependencies\n- Retry logic with exponential backoff\n- Fallback to cached health status\n- Automated recovery procedures where possible"
          },
          "response": [
            {
              "name": "Module Not Found",
              "originalRequest": {
                "method": "GET",
                "header": [],
